      "description": "Per-hole charging is a real control now (gap G3, ChargeHoleList.ts): the Charge step renders a \"Per Hole\" section, one row per hole keyed by data-hole, each with its own commit button at [data-hole=\"<id>\"] [data-action=\"charge-hole\"]. That button dispatches `charge hole:<id> explosive:<selected> amount:<amount>kg stemming:<stemming>m` from the panel's current product card / amount / stemming values (ChargeStep.chargeHole, Charge.ts) — the same three values Charge All reads, so the steppers have to be driven to the declared numbers first. 1 amount increment (5 -> 6kg) and 20 stemming increments (2.0 -> 6.0m, 0.2m per click) reach this hole's declared 6kg/6m; boomite is already the panel's default product, so no card click is needed. 6m stemming is legal against the hole's real 6m depth — createCharge (ChargePlan.ts) rejects only stemming strictly greater than depth. Amount steps by 1kg (data-field=\"amount\", clamped to the selected product's [minChargeKg, maxChargeKg]); stemming steps by 0.2m with a 0.5m floor (data-field=\"stemming\", Charge.ts adjustStemming). Both are plain instance fields on ChargeStep with no reset path, so they carry over from the previous charge step in the same page session — asserted before each commit rather than assumed.",
      "role": "player",
      "expect": {
        "equals": {
          "chargedCount": 1
        },
        "note": "first of four decks — only this hole is charged so far"
